preConditionHook:
// BROOKS'S STAIRS (T26-01, the chapter named for it) -- a broad channel
// trend that climbs in steps. LONG is the BULL stairs: minStairs successive
// confirmed swing pivots on BOTH series, each newer swing low above the one
// before it AND each newer swing high above the one before it, with the
// OVERLAP that separates stairs from a plain trend of higher highs and higher
// lows -- each new leg's swing low trades back BELOW the previous leg's swing
// high, i.e. the breakout retraces past its own breakout point. SHORT is the
// mirror bear stairs.
//
// minStairs is the number of PIVOTS per series the merged pseudocode asks for
// ('for k in 1..minStairs-1', comparing pivot k against pivot k+1), so the
// default 3 is three pivots and TWO step comparisons. It is clamped to 2..3:
// three pivot slots per series are carried, which is what the default needs
// and what the pivot window can be relied on to hold.
//
// The merged parameter maxLegs(6) is NOT carried. Nothing in the rule ranges
// over more legs than minStairs, so an input capping a range that does not
// exist would only waste an optimizer dimension. pivotLookback(40) replaces
// it -- the merged parameters omitted the window, which is EL's Length and is
// load-bearing here because it bounds how old the oldest of the three pivots
// may be. 40 is ThreePushPattern's default, the corpus's three-pivot window.
//
// THE PIVOT SCAN IS INLINED rather than calling SwingHigh / SwingLow at
// Occurrence 1, 2 and 3. The register's swinghigh and swinglow rows are
// VERIFIED but list Occurrence 3+ explicitly as UNMEASURED, and the third
// pivot is exactly what makes this stairs rather than one leg. Slices B01 and
// B02 blocked this rule on that; the inlined scan is the route ratified for a
// third or later pivot, since plain EL loops and comparisons are themselves
// registered and the scan reproduces the MEASURED pivot test exactly
// (EL_Swing_Probe.txt / el_swing_output1.txt, @ES 60 min):
//
//   * the pivot bar is AT OR ABOVE the pivotStrength OLDER bars and STRICTLY
//     ABOVE the pivotStrength NEWER bars, so a flat top yields exactly ONE
//     pivot, the LATER of the equal bars. Bars-ago indexing makes the SMALLER
//     index the NEWER bar, so the strict half is the k < j loop (el_gt) and
//     the at-or-above half the k > j loop (el_ge);
//   * the confirmation lag is exactly pivotStrength bars, which is why the
//     scan starts at j = pivotStrength -- that lag is what makes it
//     lookahead-safe;
//   * candidate offsets run 0 .. Length - 1 from the current bar INCLUSIVE,
//     so j stops at pivotLookback - 1, while the neighbourhood test reaches
//     pivotStrength bars PAST the window: deepest bar touched is
//     pivotLookback - 1 + pivotStrength;
//   * scanning newest-first and recording the first three hits reproduces
//     Occurrence 1, 2, 3;
//   * the comparisons carry the 2.22e-12 relational tolerance, hence el_gt /
//     el_ge / el_lt / el_le rather than raw > and >=;
//   * the prices are initialised to the -1 SENTINEL and every use is gated on
//     the counts reaching needPiv -- -1 as a PRICE sits under every real one;
//   * the low side's TIE sense is the mirror of the measured high-side rule
//     rather than an observation, as the swinglow row records.
//
// There is no WFSafe_SwingHigh in the MultiWalk library, so plain EL governs.
// Written WITHOUT an early break, matching the EL twin statement for
// statement: Break is not a registered EasyLanguage word, so the twin's loops
// run to the end and the `< 3` guards stop a fourth pivot being recorded.
//
// No scratch is declared at hook scope -- every value below is a
// localVariables entry -- because this rule may be placed twice in one
// strategy and its hooks emitted twice into the one class.
//
// ShrinkingStairs is deliberately a SEPARATE rule and is not inlined here: a
// stairs trend can have growing, equal or shrinking steps, and only the
// shrinking case carries Brooks's warning. AND the two in a pane.
nHiPiv = 0;
nLoPiv = 0;
hiPx1 = -1.0;
hiPx2 = -1.0;
hiPx3 = -1.0;
loPx1 = -1.0;
loPx2 = -1.0;
loPx3 = -1.0;
for (int j = (int)pivotStrength; j <= (int)pivotLookback - 1; ++j) {
    bool okHi = true;
    bool okLo = true;
    for (int k = j - (int)pivotStrength; k < j; ++k) {
        if (!el_gt(high[j], high[k])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_lt(low[j], low[k])) okLo = false;
    }
    for (int k = j + 1; k <= j + (int)pivotStrength; ++k) {
        if (!el_ge(high[j], high[k])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_le(low[j], low[k])) okLo = false;
    }
    if (okHi && nHiPiv < 3) {
        nHiPiv = nHiPiv + 1;
        if (nHiPiv == 1) hiPx1 = high[j];
        if (nHiPiv == 2) hiPx2 = high[j];
        if (nHiPiv == 3) hiPx3 = high[j];
    }
    if (okLo && nLoPiv < 3) {
        nLoPiv = nLoPiv + 1;
        if (nLoPiv == 1) loPx1 = low[j];
        if (nLoPiv == 2) loPx2 = low[j];
        if (nLoPiv == 3) loPx3 = low[j];
    }
}
needPiv = (int)minStairs;
if (needPiv > 3) needPiv = 3;
if (needPiv < 2) needPiv = 2;
stairsUp = (nHiPiv >= needPiv) && (nLoPiv >= needPiv);
stairsDn = stairsUp;
if (!el_gt(loPx1, loPx2)) stairsUp = false;
if (!el_gt(hiPx1, hiPx2)) stairsUp = false;
if (!el_lt(loPx1, hiPx2)) stairsUp = false;
if (!el_lt(loPx1, loPx2)) stairsDn = false;
if (!el_lt(hiPx1, hiPx2)) stairsDn = false;
if (!el_gt(hiPx1, loPx2)) stairsDn = false;
if (needPiv >= 3) {
    if (!el_gt(loPx2, loPx3)) stairsUp = false;
    if (!el_gt(hiPx2, hiPx3)) stairsUp = false;
    if (!el_lt(loPx2, hiPx3)) stairsUp = false;
    if (!el_lt(loPx2, loPx3)) stairsDn = false;
    if (!el_lt(hiPx2, hiPx3)) stairsDn = false;
    if (!el_gt(hiPx2, loPx3)) stairsDn = false;
}
